<!--
  More apps / Popover — read from the live file on 2026-10-11.

  WHY THIS IS A FILE OF ITS OWN

  The same reason as 398-26305.xml: it belongs to the page, and the page
  export does not contain it. Searched for by name against 70-28.xml, which
  holds 7,344 frames: "More apps / Popover" returns nothing, and the only
  match for "More apps" is `More apps / opens inward` — the LIST design this
  component replaces.

  So the page export is stale for this component and this file is
  authoritative for it. A full re-export remains owed and does not block it.

  WHAT IT REPLACES, AND WHY THAT MATTERS TO A READER

  `More apps / opens inward` is a 248-wide list of names. This is a 448-wide
  popover with a search field and a four-column grid of applications. They are
  not versions of one design; the owner's ruling of 2026-10-11 (ADR 0103)
  changed what the surface is — from the applications that overflowed to every
  pinned and open application — and this is the design for that.

  **Anything measured off `More apps / opens inward` is measuring the old
  surface.** `AN_OVERFLOW_PANEL_IS_WIDE = 248` in `alo_dock::measures` came
  from it and is superseded by the 448 here.

  THE HEIGHTS ARE CAPS, NOT MEASUREMENTS OF THESE FRAMES

  The owner stated them separately from the file, on 2026-10-11:

    the entire popover, including heading, search and footer   536
    the scrollable application-list viewport                   336
    the reference width                                        448

  Every state below is 448 x 536 because each is drawn at the cap. **Sixty
  applications must scroll inside the same bounded viewport**, and on a
  shorter output the list viewport shrinks further so that the whole popover
  fits. So a reader must not take 336 as "the height of the list": it is the
  largest the list may be.

  WHERE IT SITS, from `01 · More apps / Bottom · With minimised windows`
  (408:28177, a 1440x960 frame)

    popover            x 668, y 312, 448 x 536   -> bottom edge at 848
    Dock / Bottom      x 164, y 860, 952 x  76   -> top edge at 860

  **12 between them**, which is the gap the owner names. The minimised-window
  panel in the same frame is at x 1172, 244 wide, so the popover's right edge
  at 1116 clears it by 56.
-->
